                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi Kasun, thanks for the patch. I have a few comments inline."
                },
                {
                    "file": "CHANGELOG.md",
                    "line": 25,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "One way or the other this can be the same as the commit message subject. I'd prefer we be this specific in the commit message subject if we can (you can use `gitlint-ignore: T1` in the commit trailer to disable the lint on the subject length if necessary)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "CHANGELOG.md",
                    "line": 25,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kasun Athukorala",
                        "email": "kasunath@google.com",
                        "username": "kasunathg"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/base.h",
                    "line": 835,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "The ordering of parameters doesn't match the documentation, and splitting `msg` from `payload_length` feels quite wrong. Let's please to keep things that go together together and order the arguments as you've ordered their documentation above."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/base.h",
                    "line": 835,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kasun Athukorala",
                        "email": "kasunath@google.com",
                        "username": "kasunathg"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/base.c",
                    "line": 839,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "See comment on the header regarding parameter ordering."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/base.c",
                    "line": 839,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kasun Athukorala",
                        "email": "kasunath@google.com",
                        "username": "kasunathg"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/base.c",
                    "line": 841,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you please rebase this series to the tip of main? Yesterday we merged [msgbuf: Define a separate msgbuf structure for encode/decode function](https://github.com/openbmc/libpldm/commit/7a8d932bc3cd30a0869b2e5cfd38c1b87019cffb) which gives us const-correctness for the msgbuf APIs. In the process it reworked the types and macros involved.\n\nYou'll need to switch this to:\n\n```\nPLDM_MSGBUF_RO_DEFINE_P(buf);\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/base.c",
                    "line": 841,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kasun Athukorala",
                        "email": "kasunath@google.com",
                        "username": "kasunathg"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/base.c",
                    "line": 858,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "You can skip this check as you don't subsequently use the value of `req->requester_part_size` in the function implementation."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/base.c",
                    "line": 858,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kasun Athukorala",
                        "email": "kasunath@google.com",
                        "username": "kasunathg"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "tests/dsp/base.cpp",
                    "line": 1762,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Please avoid `reinterpret_cast<>()` as suggested by clang-tidy. Instead we have `PLDM_MSG_DEFINE_P()`:\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/libpldm/blob/main/include/libpldm/base.h#L246-L260\n\nPlease fix throughout."
                },
